    "headline": "Attrition Risk Model Shows Weak Predictive Power but Identifies Key Feature Gaps in Critical Risk Tiers",
    "key_insight_1": "The Random Forest model, while exhibiting weak overall predictive accuracy (0.4757), indicates that 'Employee_Health_Insurance_Coverage' (0.00273 AUC drop) and 'Employee_Stock_Options' (0.002545 AUC drop) are the most influential features in predicting attrition. This suggests that benefits and equity are primary considerations for employees, even within a model with limited predictive capacity.",
